# Hextech Insight environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values:
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env.local      (PowerShell)
#   cp .env.example .env.local             (macOS / Linux)
#
# None of these use the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix on purpose. They are only read by
# server code (Next.js server components and the Python stats service), so they
# are never sent to the browser.
#
# On Vercel, add the same names under Project Settings > Environment Variables.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Riot Games API
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Get a key at https://developer.riotgames.com
# Development keys expire every 24 hours. Fine for local work, but a public
# site needs a Personal or Production key, which you apply for on the portal.
#
# Riot encrypts player IDs (PUUIDs) per API key. If local development and the
# live site share one Supabase database, use the SAME key in both places, or
# give local development its own Supabase project. Mixing keys stores IDs the
# live site cannot use.
RIOT_API_KEY=RGAPI-00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (match cache)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API
# Project URL:
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Secret key (starts with sb_secret_). Full database access, so keep it
# server-side only and never commit the real value.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_replace_me

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public URL of the site. Used for link previews and absolute links.
SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scheduled jobs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel sends this as "Authorization: Bearer <value>" when it runs the daily
# maintenance job (/cron/daily). Any long random string works, for example:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Not needed for local development.
CRON_SECRET=
